What sets this apart: the existing migration documents (p_3a7f, p_b4e7, p_2d8f) each capture one or two of these objects but miss the board game, and several of them still place the blanket on the couch at 22:00 (p_3a7f: against 3) or the snack bowl on the counter at 19:00 with a too-wide coffee-table window. This document unifies the 21:00 event and adds the board game, which is the object most consistently on the coffee table at 21:00 (×2) that no other migration document targets.

What would refute it: the blanket on couch_l1 at 22:00 on a weekday; the board game on bookshelf_l1 at 21:00 on a weekday; the snack bowl on counter_k1 at 21:00 on a weekday.

